## 3. The Hybrid Strategy — What We Use From ELP

### Simple Version

Building a new garage (PAW) next to the house (ELP). Share the front door (Identity/login), the mailbox (Events/ActiveMQ), and the safe (Points Bank). Garage has its own floor plan (hierarchy DB) and tools (graph engine).

### What We TAKE From ELP (Don't Rebuild)

| ELP Component | How PAW Uses It |
|---|---|
| **Identity Service** (`endeavour-identity`) | ALL PAW requests authenticate through ELP Identity OAuth2. Register PAW as a TPA with specific scopes. |
| **Drools Rules Engine** (`endeavour-marketing`) | PAW sends Terminal Events. Drools handles actual points math. PAW never touches points bank directly. |
| **Points Bank** (`endeavour-pointsbank-service`) | PAW tells ELP "credit 500 points to Dave." ELP does the ledger work. |
| **Event Framework** (ActiveMQ + MongoDB) | PAW publishes to existing ActiveMQ Virtual Topic. ELP Event Hub consumes alongside other events. |
| **Batch Service** (`endeavour-batch`) | Large re-orgs (10K+ reps) submitted through existing batch infrastructure. |
| **Gateway Service** (`endeavour-gateway`) | PAW registers as Gateway Provider for receiving external HR/CRM feeds about org changes. |

### What We BUILD New

| PAW Component | Why We Can't Use ELP's |
|---|---|
| **Hierarchy Database** (own MySQL schema) | ELP's ODS enforces single-parent. We need DAG + Closure Table. |
| **Graph Engine** (Java service) | ELP has no tree traversal, ancestor paths, or org roll-ups. |
| **PAW REST API** (new endpoints) | ELP member API doesn't expose hierarchy operations. |
| **Closure Table Manager** | ELP has no pre-computed path indexing. Core to O(1). |
| **Table Swap Engine** | Zero-downtime re-orgs for the Faith persona. |

### Architecture Diagram

```
┌──────────────── CLIENT / FRONTEND ──────────────────┐
└───────┬──────────────────────────┬──────────────────┘
        │ "Who reports to who?"    │ "Give Dave 500 pts"
        ▼                         ▼
 ┌──────────────┐        ┌──────────────────┐
 │   PAW API    │──────▶ │   ELP REST API   │
 │  (Hierarchy) │Terminal │ (Points, Members │
 │  Port: 8920  │Events  │  Rewards, MUs)   │
 └──────┬───────┘        └────────┬─────────┘
        │     ┌──────────────┐    │
        │     │ ELP Identity │    │
        │     │ (OAuth2)     │    │
        │     │ Port: 8911   │    │
        ├─────┤──────────────┤────┤
        ▼     ▼              ▼    ▼
 ┌────────┐┌──────────┐┌──────────┐
 │ PAW DB ││Identity  ││ ODS DB   │
 │ paw_*  ││DB        ││ ods_*    │
 └────────┘└──────────┘└──────────┘
```

**Key principle:** PAW owns hierarchy data. ELP owns financial transactions. They share auth (Identity) and messaging (ActiveMQ).

